{{!-- The thesis, as a full-width band directly under the hero:
the words sit as faint ghosts and ink in ONE BY ONE as the band
crosses the viewport.

The quote stays a single translatable string — assets/js/quote-fill.js
splits it into words at runtime and hands each one its own slice of
the scroll, because translating the sentence one word at a time
would hand translators a pile of disconnected fragments. The script only splits when the browser
has scroll-driven animations AND the visitor allows motion; any
other case leaves the paragraph exactly as Ghost rendered it, in
full colour, which is also what a no-JS visitor gets. --}}
<section class="outer scroll-quote relative">
    <div class="bg-dots bg-fade-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="inner relative">
        <figure>
            <span class="kicker scroll-quote-kicker">{{> "icons/sparkles"}} {{t "The one idea behind all of this"}}</span>
            <blockquote>
                <span class="scroll-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span>
                <p class="scroll-quote-fill" data-word-fill>{{t "AI will come. Selling, and doing business, will never stop — it will only change shape."}}</p>
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>
                {{t "So the only durable skill is being able to solve a business problem in any era. That is what this whole site is practice for — and why I'm learning it in public."}}
                <a class="scroll-quote-link" href="{{@site.url}}/about/">{{t "The longer version"}} {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a>
            </figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>
